<SiteLayout title="About HaloForge Labs | Halowin Bubo" description="HaloForge Labs builds Halowin Bubo, an open-source local LLM server for Windows. See what it builds on and where the name comes from.">
  <span class="eyebrow">HaloForge Labs</span>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="intro">HaloForge Labs builds Halowin Bubo. This page says what it is built on, where the name comes from and whose work we use. <a href="/bubo/">Read about Halowin Bubo</a> or <a href="/docs/">open the documentation</a>.</p>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <section class="article-body"><h2>Built on gufo</h2><p>Bubo is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/gufo">gufo</a>, the open-source LLM server. The gufo authors wrote the upstream server and release it under the MIT license. The Windows port comes from pixmaate’s gufo fork.</p><h2>The name</h2><p>Halowin joins Halo, from Strix Halo, and Windows. Bubo is a genus of owls, and gufo is the Italian word for owl, so the whole family takes its name from the same bird.</p><p>The owl in our logo is the Egyptian hieroglyph for owl (G17), drawn from the Noto Sans Egyptian Hieroglyphs font under the SIL Open Font License. The text of this site is set in ET Book, by Dmitry Krasny, Bonnie Scranton and Edward Tufte, under the MIT license.</p></section>
    <aside class="margin-note"><span class="eyebrow">Source and support</span><p><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo">Source code</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/issues">Report an issue</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases">Releases</a></p></aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
